We can create the following script and attach it as a component to any object
that we want to preserve:
1 public class DontDestroy : MonoBehaviour {
2 void Awake () {
3 DontDestroyOnLoad ( gameObject ) ;
4 }
5 }
Note that gameObject or transform.gameObject is a reference to the game object that
contains this component. For keeping data, we can have a game object with
the following script attached:
1 public class GameControl : MonoBehaviour {
2 // Singleton . Accessible from ANY script !
3 public static GameControl control ;
4 public int health ;
5
6 void Awake () {
7 if ( control == null ) {
8 DontDestroyOnLoad ( gameObject ) ;
9 control = this ;
10 } else if ( control != this ) {
11 Destroy ( gameObject ) ;
12 }
13 }
14 }
Each scene has a game object with this script attached. The object is persistent
between scenes and can be referenced from any one of them.
